# context/lib/calendar.brix -- the calfour and calfive calendar, fused into one descriptor.
# Stamp: 20261018.211159. Status: living. Read beside rota-base.brix, rota.brix and rota-of-fifteen.brix.
#
# One count drives both rings. It is git rev-list --count HEAD, read once, never carried in a name.
#
# base count_source git rev-list --count HEAD
#
# calfour -- the eight-round orbit, nested by fours. Arithmetic lives in construction/calfour.sh.
# calfour round_rule (count - 1) mod 8 + 1
# calfour orbit_rule (count - 1) div 8 + 1
# calfour quest_rule ((count - 1) div 8) mod 4 + 1
# calfour journey_rule ((count - 1) div 32) mod 4 + 1
# calfour equinox_rule ((count - 1) div 512) + 1
#
# calfive -- the fifteen-round orbit, composed from the shared base, rota-base.brix. Its rows live in rota-of-fifteen.brix.
# calfive base rota-base.brix
# calfive round_rule ((count - 1) mod 15) + 1
# calfive rows context/lib/rota-of-fifteen.brix
#
# calendar_record.sh reads the calfive sign from rota-of-fifteen.brix, so that file stays the one place its rows live.
# This page names the two rings beside each other. It does not rewire any script; that is a separate, witnessed change.
